  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing the mean difference between outcomes and a reference value (zero in this case), then comparing the weighted differences. Both lotteries have the same expected value (2700 Euros), so the mean differences are equal. The reason would lead to indifference. However, the individual's justification centers on the 90% probability being more important than the higher sum with lower probability — a focus on probability, not on differences from a reference value or their weighted probabilities. There is no mention of differences from zero, nor of evaluating mean differences. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason as defined. The reasoning process described is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason. The individual used a different criterion (emphasis on probability over magnitude), not the rule involving differences from a reference value and their weighted importance. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
